# The whole .rafters/ directory is tool-managed: config.rafters.json is rewritten
# by `rafters add`, tokens/ by Studio, output/ by the exporters. None is authored.
apps/demo/.rafters/
apps/lab/.rafters/
plugin/bin/

# Installed component surface -- written by `rafters add`, not authored here.
#
# The repo already declares these read-only: pre-edit.sh denies edits to
# components/ui and lib/primitives with "installed by rafters, fix your
# consuming code or file upstream". Their formatting belongs to the registry
# the same way their content does, so the format check has no standing over
# them either.
#
# There is also a concrete reason they will never pass: `add` rewrites import
# specifiers for the consumer's configured directories, and a rewrite that
# SHORTENS a path (../../lib/contract -> @/lib/contract) can carry a line back
# under printWidth without anything reformatting it. The content is a string
# inside JSON from the registry read to the disk write, so no seam in that
# pipeline can notice. A correctly formatted source lands here formatted for a
# path it no longer has. Full diagnosis: legion reflect 01a02866.
#
# Paths are the ones each app's .rafters/config.rafters.json declares as
# rafters-written, plus the substrate dirs that ship alongside them.
apps/demo/src/components/ui/
apps/demo/src/composites/
apps/demo/src/hooks/
apps/demo/src/lib/
apps/lab/src/components/ui/
apps/lab/src/composites/
apps/lab/src/lib/
